02:01 I lifted up my eyes, and saw, and, behold, a man with a measuring line in his hand.
02:02 Then said I, Where go you? He said to me, To measure Yerushalayim, to see what is the breadth of it, and what is the length of it.
02:03 Behold, the angel who talked with me went forth, and another angel went out to meet him,
02:04 and said to him, Run, speak to this young man, saying, Yerushalayim shall be inhabited as villages without walls, by reason of the multitude of men and cattle therein.
02:05 For I, says HaSHEM, will be to her a wall of fire round about, and I will be the glory in the midst of her.
02:06 Ho, ho, flee from the land of the north, says HaSHEM; for I have spread you abroad as the four winds of the sky, says HaSHEM.
02:07 Ho Tzion, escape, you who dwell with the daughter of Bavel.
02:08 For thus says HaSHEM-Tzva'ot: After glory has he sent me to the nations which plundered you; for he who touches you touches the apple of his eye.
02:09 For, behold, I will shake my hand over them, and they shall be a spoil to those who served them; and you shall know that HaSHEM-Tzva'ot has sent me.
02:14 Sing and rejoice, daughter of Tzion; for, behold, I come, and I will dwell in the midst of you, says HaSHEM.
02:15 Many nations shall join themselves to HaSHEM in that day, and shall be my people; and I will dwell in the midst of you, and you shall know that HaSHEM-Tzva'ot has sent me to you.
02:16 HaSHEM shall inherit Yehudah as his portion in the holy land, and shall yet choose Yerushalayim.
02:17 Be silent, all flesh, before HaSHEM; for he is waked up out of his holy habitation.  
03:01 He showed me Yehoshua the Cohen Gadol standing before the angel of HaSHEM, and Hasatan standing at his right hand to be his adversary.
03:02 HaSHEM said to Hasatan, HaSHEM rebuke you, Hasatan; yes, HaSHEM that has chosen Yerushalayim rebuke you: is not this a brand plucked out of the fire?
03:03 Now Yehoshua was clothed with filthy garments, and was standing before the angel.
03:04 He answered and spoke to those who stood before him, saying, Take the filthy garments from off him. To him he said, Behold, I have caused your iniquity to pass from you, and I will clothe you with rich clothing.
03:05 I said, Let them set a clean mitre on his head. So they set a clean mitre on his head, and clothed him with garments; and the angel of HaSHEM was standing by.
03:06 The angel of HaSHEM protested to Yehoshua, saying,
03:07 Thus says HaSHEM-Tzva'ot: If you will walk in my ways, and if you will keep my charge, then you also shall judge my house, and shall also keep my courts, and I will give you a place of access among these who stand by.
03:08 Hear now, Yehoshua the Cohen Gadol, you and your fellows who sit before you; for they are men who are a sign: for, behold, I will bring forth my servant the Branch.
03:09 For, behold, the stone that I have set before Yehoshua; on one stone are seven eyes: behold, I will engrave the engraving of it, says HaSHEM-Tzva'ot, and I will remove the iniquity of that land in one day.
03:10 In that day, says HaSHEM-Tzva'ot, shall you invite every man his neighbor under the vine and under the fig-tree.  
04:01 The angel who talked with me came again, and waked me, as a man who is wakened out of his sleep.
04:02 He said to me, What see you? I said, I have seen, and, behold, a lampstand all of gold, with its bowl on the top of it, and its seven lamps thereon; there are seven pipes to each of the lamps, which are on the top of it;
04:03 and two olive-trees by it, one on the right side of the bowl, and the other on the left side of it.
04:04 I answered and spoke to the angel who talked with me, saying, What are these, my lord?
04:05 Then the angel who talked with me answered me, Don't you know what these are? I said, No, my lord.
04:06 Then he answered and spoke to me, saying, This is the word of HaSHEM to Zerubbavel, saying, Not by might, nor by power, but by my Spirit, says HaSHEM-Tzva'ot.
04:07 Who are you, great mountain? before Zerubbavel you shall become a plain; and he shall bring forth the top stone with shouts of Grace, grace, to it.
04:08 Moreover the word of HaSHEM came to me, saying,
04:09 The hands of Zerubbavel have laid the foundation of this house; his hands shall also finish it; and you shall know that HaSHEM-Tzva'ot has sent me to you.
04:10 For who has despised the day of small things? for these seven shall rejoice, and shall see the plummet in the hand of Zerubbavel; these are the eyes of HaSHEM, which run back and forth through the whole earth.
04:11 Then answered I, and said to him, What are these two olive-trees on the right side of the lampstand and on the left side of it?
04:12 I answered the second time, and said to him, What are these two olive-branches, which are beside the two golden spouts, that empty the golden oil out of themselves?
04:13 He answered me and said, "Don't you know what these are?" I said, No, my lord.
04:14 Then said he, These are the two anointed ones, that stand by the L-rd of the whole earth.  
14:01 Behold, a day of HaSHEM comes, when your spoil shall be divided in the midst of you.
14:02 For I will gather all nations against Yerushalayim to battle; and the city shall be taken, and the houses rifled, and the women ravished; and half of the city shall go forth into captivity, and the residue of the people shall not be cut off from the city.
14:03 Then shall HaSHEM go forth, and fight against those nations, as when he fought in the day of battle.
14:04 His feet shall stand in that day on the Mount of Olives, which is before Yerushalayim on the east; and the Mount of Olives shall be cleft in the midst of it toward the east and toward the west, and there shall be a very great valley; and half of the mountain shall remove toward the north, and half of it toward the south.
14:05 You shall flee by the valley of my mountains; for the valley of the mountains shall reach to Atzel; yes, you shall flee, like as you fled from before the earthquake in the days of `Uzziyah king of Yehudah; and HaSHEM my G-D shall come, and all the holy ones with you.
14:06 It shall happen in that day, that there shall not be light; the bright ones shall withdraw themselves:
14:07 but it shall be one day which is known to HaSHEM; not day, and not night; but it shall come to pass, that at evening time there shall be light.
14:08 It shall happen in that day, that living waters shall go out from Yerushalayim; half of them toward the eastern sea, and half of them toward the western sea: in summer and in winter shall it be.
14:09 HaSHEM shall be King over all the earth: in that day shall HaSHEM be one, and his name one.
14:10 All the land shall be made like the `Aravah, from Geva to Rimmon south of Yerushalayim; and she shall be lifted up, and shall dwell in her place, from Binyamin's gate to the place of the first gate, to the corner gate, and from the tower of Chanan'el to the king's wine-presses.
14:11 Men shall dwell therein, and there shall be no more curse; but Yerushalayim shall dwell safely.
14:12 This shall be the plague wherewith HaSHEM will strike all the peoples who have warred against Yerushalayim: their flesh shall consume away while they stand on their feet, and their eyes shall consume away in their sockets, and their tongue shall consume away in their mouth.
14:13 It shall happen in that day, that a great tumult from HaSHEM shall be among them; and they shall lay hold everyone on the hand of his neighbor, and his hand shall rise up against the hand of his neighbor.
14:14 Yehudah also shall fight at Yerushalayim; and the wealth of all the nations round about shall be gathered together, gold, and silver, and clothing, in great abundance.
14:15 So shall be the plague of the horse, of the mule, of the camel, and of the donkey, and of all the animals that shall be in those camps, as that plague.
14:16 It shall happen, that everyone who is left of all the nations that came against Yerushalayim shall go up from year to year to worship the King, HaSHEM-Tzva'ot, and to keep the feast of booths.
14:17 It shall be, that whoever of all the families of the earth doesn't go up to Yerushalayim to worship the King, HaSHEM-Tzva'ot, on them there shall be no rain.
14:18 If the family of Mitzrayim doesn't go up, and doesn't come, neither shall it be on them; there shall be the plague wherewith HaSHEM will strike the nations that don't go up to keep the feast of booths.
14:19 This shall be the punishment of Mitzrayim, and the punishment of all the nations that don't go up to keep the feast of booths.
14:20 In that day shall there be on the bells of the horses, HOLY TO YAHWEH; and the pots in HaSHEM's house shall be like the bowls before the altar.
14:21 Yes, every pot in Yerushalayim and in Yehudah shall be holy to HaSHEM-Tzva'ot; and all those who sacrifice shall come and take of them, and boil therein: and in that day there shall be no more a Cana`ani in the house of HaSHEM-Tzva'ot.  
